//Configure how the recipe edition behaves.//

----------

!! Photos

Photos add visual richness, but sourcing and attributing public images takes effort.  Pick the option that matches how you plan to work — edit forms and the Recipe Box dashboard adapt accordingly.  Recipes and ingredients always display any photos that are attached, regardless of mode.

<div class="tc-recipe-photo-mode-options">
<div><$radio tiddler="$:/config/community/recipes/photos" field="text" value="none" default="own"> Don't use photos</$radio></div>
<div><$radio tiddler="$:/config/community/recipes/photos" field="text" value="own" default="own"> Use my own photos (no attribution required)</$radio></div>
<div><$radio tiddler="$:/config/community/recipes/photos" field="text" value="attributed" default="own"> Use public photos with attribution</$radio></div>
</div>

----------

!! Extra fields

These fields appear in the metadata strip at the top of each recipe view, and are routed to a placeholder-aware editor in the field list when you author a recipe.  Edit a row to change its caption, placeholder hint, or display template; remove a row to drop the field from the strip and the editor cascade.

<table class="tc-recipe-extra-fields-table">
<thead>
<tr><th>Field name</th><th>Caption</th><th>Placeholder</th><th></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<$list filter="[all[shadows+tiddlers]tag[$:/tags/community/recipes/extra-field]]" variable="extraField">
<tr>
<td><$text text={{{ [<extraField>get[field-name]] }}}/></td>
<td><$text text={{{ [<extraField>get[caption]] }}}/></td>
<td><$text text={{{ [<extraField>get[placeholder]] }}}/></td>
<td>
<$button class="tc-btn-invisible">
<$action-sendmessage $message="tm-edit-tiddler" $param=<<extraField>>/>
edit
</$button>
&nbsp;
<$button class="tc-btn-invisible">
<$action-deletetiddler $tiddler=<<extraField>>/>
remove
</$button>
</td>
</tr>
</$list>
</tbody>
</table>

<$button>
<$action-sendmessage $message="tm-new-tiddler" title="$:/community/recipes/extra-fields/new-field" tags="$:/tags/community/recipes/extra-field" field-name="" caption="" placeholder=""/>
Add a new field
</$button>
